.SH "GLOBAL"
.SH "NAME"
.PP
\fIglobal\fP \- hold global server properties

.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP
\fIglobal\fP holds global server properties, like the prometheus metrics port and root directory.
It only implements the \fB\fCSetupper\fR interface and it's not a handler and you can not use it as such.

.SH "SYNTAX"
.PP
.RS

.nf
root DIRECTORY
prometheus ADDRRES
debug

.fi
.RE

.IP \(bu 4
with \fIroot\fP \fBDIRECTORY\fP is the directory to use as the root directory for the server. Any relative path names will
get this directory prefixed.
.IP \(bu 4
with \fIdebug\fP the global log level is to debug.
.IP \(bu 4
The \fIprometheus\fP property allows setting the listening \fBADDRESS\fP.


.SH "EXAMPLES"
.PP
.RS

.nf
{
    root /var/lib/testserv
}

.fi
.RE
